flare Clef Flash</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare Clef Omni</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kev 4B</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tev1 4B experimental (OpenRouter native adapter)</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drex v1.5</th><td style="background:#c6e9b4;color:#000000">2/8 (25.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Luna 6 Decisions</th><td style="background:#c6e9b4;color:#000000">2/8 (25.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Solar Decide Flash</th><td style="background:#c6e9b4;color:#000000">2/8 (25.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sonnet 5.5 — no thinking, JSON-choice</th><td style="background:#edf8b1;color:#000000">1/8 (12.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ScaleDown Classify-1</th><td style="background:#edf8b1;color:#000000">1/8 (12.5%)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details></article><article class="category-card" id="category-F30"><h4>Checking overlapping operations</h4><p class="category-meta">F30 · 8 questions</p><p>Decide whether overlapping operations and their reported results can fit a permitted one-at-a-time order that respects the specified timing and object rules.</p><p class="example"><b>Example:</b> Two processes read and change the same stored value. Could their reported results fit an allowed one-at-a-time order?</p><p><b>Highest observed:</b> GPT-6 Sol (LLM, none) · 7/8 (87.5%)</p><details><summary>All 26 routes in this category</summary><div class="ranked-category"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Correct / questions (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">GPT-6 Sol — no reasoning</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Respan Span-02</th><td style="background:#1d90c0;color:#000000">5/8 (62.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sonnet 5.5 — no thinking, JSON-choice</th><td style="background:#1d90c0;color:#000000">5/8 (62.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">kettei-fat</th><td style="background:#1d90c0;color:#000000">5/8 (62.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mercury Decide</th><td style="background:#1d90c0;color:#000000">5/8 (62.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare Clef</th><td style="background:#1d90c0;color:#000000">5/8 (62.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Perplexity Decider v1.2</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">d3-turbo</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jev 1.14</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jev 1.13</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Qwen3.8-Max — none, Hyper Charm</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Microsoft-Decision-1</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drex v2.0</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drex v1.5</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Solar Decide Flash</th><td style="background:#40b5c4;color:#000000">4/8 (50.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Nimble v4 Max</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Liquid d1-ultra</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Amos 1 Large</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Liquid d1</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Perplexity Decider Flash v1.2</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kev 4B</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Luna 6 Decisions</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tev1 4B experimental (OpenRouter native adapter)</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare Clef Flash</th><td style="background:#c6e9b4;color:#000000">2/8 (25.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare Clef Omni</th><td style="background:#c6e9b4;color:#000000">2/8 (25.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ScaleDown Classify-1</th><td style="background:#edf8b1;color:#000000">1/8 (12.5%)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details></article><article class="category-card" id="category-F31"><h4>Detecting secret-information leaks</h4><p class="category-meta">F31 · 8 questions</p><p>Check whether changing a protected secret can change an observable result in a way the stated policy forbids.</p><p class="example"><b>Example:</b> If public inputs stay the same, could public output distinguish two secret values that the policy says must remain indistinguishable?</p><p><b>Highest observed:</b> GPT-6 Sol (LLM, none) · 8/8 (100.0%)</p><details><summary>All 26 routes in this category</summary><div class="ranked-category"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Correct / questions (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">GPT-6 Sol — no reasoning</th><td style="background:#081d58;color:#ffffff">8/8 (100.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sonnet 5.5 — no thinking, JSON-choice</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Qwen3.8-Max — none, Hyper Charm</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Perplexity Decider v1.2</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Nimble v4 Max</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">d3-turbo</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Amos 1 Large</th><td style="background:#225