ssify-1</th><td style="background:#7ecdbb;color:#000000">3/8 (37.5%)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details></article></div><details><summary>View or download the full-size chart for this group</summary><div class="category-chart"><a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/uncertainty.svg"><img src="direct_additions_2026-10-20/uncertainty.png" alt="All 26 routes: Risk, strategy and system behavior; full category names, exact correct counts and percentages"></a></div><p><a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/uncertainty.png">PNG</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/uncertainty.svg">SVG</a></p></details></section><p><a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/category_scores.csv">Download the full named-category score matrix (CSV)</a>. Display names use plain language; stable category IDs and the tested data are unchanged. Examples explain the task types; they are illustrations, not additional scored questions.</p></section><section id="quality"><h2>Delivered decisions and failures</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Usable first</th><th>Wrong valid</th><th>Provider failures</th><th>Output failures</th><th>Recoveries</th><th>Eventual correct</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>GPT-6 Sol — no reasoning</th><td>1342</td><td>199</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1143</td></tr><tr><th>Respan Span-02</th><td>1342</td><td>215</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1127</td></tr><tr><th>Perplexity Decider v1.2</th><td>1341</td><td>221</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1121</td></tr><tr><th>Nimble v4 Max</th><td>1342</td><td>227</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1115</td></tr><tr><th>d3-turbo</th><td>1342</td><td>236</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1106</td></tr><tr><th>Liquid d1-ultra</th><td>1341</td><td>257</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1085</td></tr><tr><th>Amos 1 Large</th><td>1342</td><td>268</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1074</td></tr><tr><th>Sonnet 5.5 — no thinking, JSON-choice</th><td>1342</td><td>272</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1070</td></tr><tr><th>kettei-fat</th><td>1342</td><td>276</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1066</td></tr><tr><th>Jev 1.14</th><td>1342</td><td>312</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1030</td></tr><tr><th>Jev 1.13</th><td>1342</td><td>316</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1026</td></tr><tr><th>Mercury Decide</th><td>1342</td><td>325</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1017</td></tr><tr><th>Qwen3.8-Max — none, Hyper Charm</th><td>1317</td><td>350</td><td>25</td><td>0</td><td>23</td><td>971</td></tr><tr><th>Liquid d1</th><td>1342</td><td>377</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>965</td></tr><tr><th>Cloudflare Clef</th><td>1342</td><td>406</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>936</td></tr><tr><th>Perplexity Decider Flash v1.2</th><td>1286</td><td>363</td><td>56</td><td>0</td><td>56</td><td>940</td></tr><tr><th>Microsoft-Decision-1</th><td>1342</td><td>421</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>921</td></tr><tr><th>Drex v2.0</th><td>1302</td><td>387</td><td>40</td><td>0</td><td>40</td><td>933</td></tr><tr><th>Cloudflare Clef Flash</th><td>1342</td><td>482</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>860</td></tr><tr><th>Cloudflare Clef Omni</th><td>1341</td><td>481</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>861</td></tr><tr><th>Drex v1.5</th><td>1342</td><td>489</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>853</td></tr><tr><th>Kev 4B</th><td>1342</td><td>520</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>822</td></tr><tr><th>Luna 6 Decisions</th><td>1300</td><td>542</td><td>42</td><td>0</td><td>42</td><td>761</td></tr><tr><th>Tev1 4B experimental (OpenRouter native adapter)</th><td>1342</td><td>591</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>751</td></tr><tr><th>ScaleDown Classify-1</th><td>1342</td><td>792</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>550</td></tr><tr><th>Solar Decide Flash</th><td>1340</td><td>802</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>539</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Sonnet’s stopped bare-ID trial remains separate: 26/110 usable, 84 unusable. Its complete JSON-choice run is the ranked row. Qwen quota rejections remain unsuccessful deliveries in its primary denominator.</p></section><section id="image-support"><h2>Which decision models accept images?</h2><p>Current documentation declares image input for <b>16 of the 23 decision models</b>, including all three new additions. This text report assigns no image accuracy, latency or cost to them. The existing image benchmark is unchanged.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/etsabary/system-1-decision-benchmark/blob/main/IMAGE_CAPABILITIES.md">Full model-by-model capability list and sources</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/image_capabilities.json">Dated source review (JSON)</a> · <a href="https://github.com/etsabary/visual-decision-benchmark">Separate image benchmark</a></p></section><section id="method"><h2>Method, accounting and limits</h2><p>The full comparison covers 26 routes × 1342 questions = 34,892 first attempts: 23 specialized decision models and three separately labelled high-end LLM references. The same 1342 inputs, facts and five choices retain their tested order. No existing model was rerun or removed for this update. There are 35,058 selected HTTP attempts, including 166 permitted recoveries; the three October 20 runs account for 4026 first attempts and zero recoveries.</p><p>Primary scores and latency use all first attempts. A valid wrong choice is never retried. One recovery is permitted only for transport failures or HTTP 408/429/5xx; its cost is included and its response cannot replace the first attempt in the ranking. Provider failures are unsuccessful delivered decisions, not classified as wrong reasoning choices.</p><p>Median and p95 are computed from individual first-attempt times, never averages of stage medians. Timing runs from a fresh HTTPS connection through the complete response body, not time to first token. Deliberate admission, rate-limit and retry waits are excluded. The mean is also available for the three new runs. p95 is an interpolated 95th percentile, not the mean of the slowest 5%.</p><p>The October 20 additions use direct provider APIs. Amos was paced below its public 60-request/minute cap. Sqwish starter access used one active request and 2.1-second start spacing after an account-limit amendment; the first 54 successful attempts remain included. Its response latency is not batch throughput. d3-turbo used up to two in flight. Previous routes, dates, loads and quantiles are unchanged. Different protocols, hosting hardware and account conditions are not controlled away.</p><p>Among the earlier 20 decision routes, Nimble uses Bespoke directly and the others use OpenRouter with pinned providers and no fallback. Sol and Sonnet use OpenRouter; Qwen uses Hyper Charm. Sonnet requires the separately labelled JSON-choice grammar; its stopped bare-ID trial remains outside the scored comparison. Qwen requests reasoning_effort=none but has no reasoning-token telemetry. Tev1 is a decision-specialized generative model using a native adapter, not a claimed nongenerative architecture.</p><p>All three new responses named the requested model and reported zero output tokens. The hosted names do not attest immutable weights or reveal internal implementation. No explanation generation, tool use, agentic iteration or answer-dependent repair was requested. This measures System 1-style choices, not unrestricted reasoning or general intelligence.</p><p>Costs per 1000 are actual selected-run costs divided by 1342 and multiplied by 1000. Probe charges are separate. Sqwish charges come from every returned receipt and match the captured $0.06 per million input tokens; its exact full-bank charge is $0.02071056. d3-turbo and Amos used currently free public access, with no API-reported monetary charge; their metered price fields are null, not fabricated zeros. They have no cost-axis numeric point. Starter credit does not make Sqwish free.</p><p>Earlier captured charges and usage-times-tariff accounting remain unchanged. + ? means additional unreported charges, not zero. Nimble retains its recorded mixed tariffs; Hyper Charm Qwen is a prepaid-quota valuation, not a cash invoice. Verification subscriptions are outside model-inference accounting. The total is not an independently reconciled financial invoice.</p><p>This is a developing benchmark with dependent variants and uneven category sizes, not 1342 independent observations or a pristine held-out evaluation. The 37 author-development cases retain their permanent exclusion from a future held-out scored release and their separate 1305-case diagnostic. The complete developmental ranking remains 1342 questions for every route. Small score gaps do not establish a general intelligence ordering.</p><p>The construction combines the corrected 1136-question bank, 200 verified expansion questions and six additional truth-teller questions into one score. The 31 categories and their question weights are unchanged. Each of F26–F31 has eight questions, so one answer changes a category score by 12.5 percentage points. Display groups are reading aids, not additional scored categories.</p><p>All 206 expansion questions have current-revision blind Sol xhigh and different-model Opus or Argon checks, supplemented by exact computational evidence. The original bank received a targeted difficult-item audit, not independent external verification of every original question. Two retired ambiguous procedure questions are absent; their verified replacements appear once.</p><p>All question inputs remain available without answer keys. Aggregate scores, categories, usage and costs are published; answer keys, item-level correctness, certificates, verifier responses, raw account data and credentials are not. Publication validators check consistency and privacy; public aggregates cannot reproduce private-key scoring or raw-latency pooling. The dated audit receipt binds the private evidence checks.</p><p>Sixteen earlier regular-LLM configurations have only 1136-question coverage and are not extrapolated. Solar Decide remains excluded for latency; the distinct Solar Decide Flash remains included. No older published row was removed. The separate image benchmark is unchanged; documented image support is not an image score.</p></section><section id="downloads"><h2>Questions, statistics and audit</h2><p><a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/statistics.json">26-route aggregate statistics</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/model_statistics.csv">Model CSV</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/category_scores.csv">Named-category CSV</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/audit_receipt.json">Sanitized audit receipt</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/manifest.json">Release manifest</a> · <a href="direct_additions_2026-10-20/report.txt">Plain-text findings</a></p><p>Unchanged, answer-free question bank: <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.csv">CSV</a> · <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.jsonl">Exact native inputs (JSONL)</a> · <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.txt">Readable text</a>.</p></section></main></body></html>
